{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And he refused to be comforted.</b> He refused to hear words of consolation, so that the sorrow would not depart from his heart." "<b>And he said, I will go down to my son mourning to Sheol.</b> He accepted upon himself mourning for all his days, because the harm came about through him — that he sent Joseph to his brothers." "<b>And his father wept for him.</b> Isaac wept because his son accepted upon himself mourning for all his days, and thus the Shechinah would not rest upon him."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:42.415480391Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}